  "worked_solution": "In this case, we have to use the identity  \n\n$$\n1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x={csc}^{2}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{1-{cot}^{4}\u2061x}{{cot}^{2}\u2061x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}\\frac{(1-{cot}^{2}\u2061x)(1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x)}{{cot}^{2}\u2061x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}(1+{cot}^{2}\u2061x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3}{csc}^{2}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}\u2061x{|}_{\\pi /2}^{2\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-\\operatorname{cot}\u2061\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
